ct Metrics","A/B Testing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Future"},{"type":"flow","items":["Generative AI","AI-assisted analysis","Automation","AI governance"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Graduate Profile"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gather requirements from stakeholders."},{"text":"Convert business problems into structured requirements."},{"text":"Write professional user stories."},{"text":"Define acceptance criteria."},{"text":"Create process maps."},{"text":"Perform gap analysis."},{"text":"Analyse business data using SQL."},{"text":"Build dashboards using Power BI."},{"text":"Use advanced Excel."},{"text":"Understand APIs and databases."},{"text":"Work within Agile/Scrum teams."},{"text":"Use Jira and documentation tools."},{"text":"Conduct UAT."},{"text":"Present recommendations to stakeholders."},{"text":"Build 3–5 professional BA case studies."},{"text":"Complete at least one relevant internship."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Practical Path"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com Computer Applications","Business Fundamentals","Excel","SQL","Business Analysis Fundamentals","Requirements Engineering","User Stories","Process Mapping","Agile + Jira","Power BI","Python","BA Internship","Junior Business Analyst","Business Analyst","Senior BA","Lead BA / Product Analyst","Product Manager / BA Manager"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Business Analysis","SQL","Power BI","Finance/Commerce Domain Knowledge","Agile","Product Thinking","AI."],"sep":"+","label":"Best long-term combination"},{"type":"p","text":"The B.Com + Computer Applications combination is particularly valuable when the graduate targets Finance, Banking, FinTech, ERP or business-operations analysis, because they can understand both the business side and the technology side of the problem."}]}]}